The '''Guadazequias''' ({{IPA|mxi|ɡwaðaseˈkias|lang}}; {{Literal translation|valley of the sown fields}}; {{Langx|kp|Yawara Pú|4=jaguar's water}}) is the fifth-longest [[river]] on the [[Balisca|Baliscan]] island of [[Atlántida]] and the longest river with its entire length in [[Araucaria]]. The Guadalquivir is one of X major [[Navigability|navigable]] rivers in Balisca. Currently it is navigable from [[Mármoles]] to [[Bahía de los Pinos]], but in pre-colonial times it was navigable from [[Calatañazor]].

